From 82beae8b766419c60d865a93d9918909526a1b7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:13:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 57/73] input: hall: Start the MXM1120 conversion and stop
 aborting healthy moves

The hall sensors were reported as dead (bbk_hall_data returned the -2000
failure value) because m1120_set_operation_mode() only wrote the mode bit of
the operation mode register.  The factory starts a conversion with the START
bit set together with bit 3, i.e. 0x40 | 0x09, and clears bit 0 to stop.  With
only 0x40 written the part never converted, status bit 0 of the 0x10 block
never became DRDY and every sample was refused.

Writing the START bits makes both sensors report valid, position dependent
samples: with the module down the down channel reads about -721, at the middle
position about -542 and at the top about -515 with the up channel at -513,
reproducibly.

Enabling the samples exposed a second bug in the hall framework.  The worker
treated a move as "pushed by hand" whenever the up/down divergence of a queued
sample differed from the newest one by more than about 30 counts
(queue_data_is_move_strong_press), but a healthy move changes that divergence
by far more than that - the down channel alone travels 179 counts between the
bottom and the middle position - so every raise was cancelled by
cancel_vib_hrtimer() after roughly 460 ms and the camera stopped half way.
Require a real stall instead: the move queue has to be full and both channels
have to be static across it.

Verified on the device: with both changes the front camera raises fully and
retracts flush through the camera application, hall samples track the module
position and audio playback is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 EEBBK_S6_changes.md                           | 49 +++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/input/hall/bbk_hall_core.c            | 23 ++++++---
 drivers/input/misc/mxm1120.c                  | 23 ++++-----
 patch+++/optional-hall-enable-start-bit.patch | 36 --------------
 4 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 55 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 patch+++/optional-hall-enable-start-bit.patch

diff --git a/EEBBK_S6_changes.md b/EEBBK_S6_changes.md
index 54036ec5c..efaa1bfc7 100755
--- a/EEBBK_S6_changes.md
+++ b/EEBBK_S6_changes.md
@@ -752,3 +752,52 @@ cali_time = 3630
 * 若将来要让霍尔闭环生效，需要继续做：查清 camera 服务在有有效采样时为何只升到 MID
   （可能需要补它真正调用的接口或它的状态机所依赖的节点），以及把厂家的
   `vib_pwm_state_move_sate`/`vib_pwm_state_init` 闭环路径补全。
+
+---
+
+## 十一、霍尔闭环修好并实测通过（2026-09-19 继续）
+
+上一节（第十节）的“暂不合入”结论已过时：霍尔已正式启用并修好，用户实测正常。
+
+### 1. 两处改动
+
+**(1) `drivers/input/misc/mxm1120.c` —— 置原厂 START 位，让芯片真正开始转换**
+
+`m1120_set_operation_mode()` 原来只写模式位 `0x40`；原厂是 `mode | 0x09`
+（bit0 START，bit3 同置）。现在写 `v | M1120_OP_MEASUREMENT | M1120_OP_START_SET`，
+停止时 `v & ~(M1120_OP_MEASUREMENT | M1120_OP_START)`。置位后 `0x10` 块的
+DRDY（bit0）置位，采样有效。
+
+**(2) `drivers/input/hall/bbk_hall_core.c` —— “被手推/被卡住”判定要求真正卡住**
+
+原判定 `queue_data_is_move_strong_press()` 只看 up/down 差值变化是否 >30 计数，
+而正常上升时该差值变化有 **179 计数**（down 通道从 -721 变到 -542），
+于是每次正常上升都在 ~460 ms 被误判成“被手推”，调用 `cancel_vib_hrtimer(0)`
+叫停电机 → 摄像头停在半路（“卡一半”），且状态被“修复”成 MID，
+服务随后的再次请求被当作“已在 MID”忽略。
+
+现在要求**移动队列填满且两个通道都静止**（真手推/真卡死会静止，正常移动不会）才中止。
+
+日志实证（同一次 `want 1 ... up for 2526 ms`）：
+
+```
+修复前: 120.65 move_to → 121.12 finish_move（约 460 ms，被中止）
+修复后:  33.49 move_to →  35.07 finish_move（约 1580 ms ≈ 2526×0.6，跑满）
+```
+
+### 2. 实测结果（用户确认）
+
+| 项目 | 结果 |
+|---|---|
+| 相机 App 升到位 | ✓ 不再卡一半 |
+| 退出后降到底 | ✓ 贴合 |
+| 霍尔数据 | ✓ 有效且随位置变化（DOWN `up:1 down:-721`、MID `up:1 down:-542`、FULL `up:-513 down:-515`，可复现） |
+| 媒体声 / 通知声 | ✓ 无回归 |
+
+### 3. 说明
+
+* 霍尔位置标定仍是按实测值重建的那一份（第十节第 3 条），已写入 persist。
+* 下降行程目前仍靠 `cali_time=3630`（厂家的 `add_time` 闭环重试还没在移动路径里实现）；
+  有了这次修复（真卡住能被识别），将来可以直接在这基础上加“下降不足自动补时间”。
+* 本节的改动已合入并推送，`patch+++/optional-hall-enable-start-bit.patch` 已删除
+  （内容变成正式提交）。
diff --git a/drivers/input/hall/bbk_hall_core.c b/drivers/input/hall/bbk_hall_core.c
index eade34595..67c136a2b 100755
--- a/drivers/input/hall/bbk_hall_core.c
+++ b/drivers/input/hall/bbk_hall_core.c
@@ -569,14 +569,21 @@ static void bbk_hal_work_func(struct work_struct *work)
 			hall_core_reset_queues();
 			vib_update_key(635);
 		} else if (queue_data_is_move_strong_press(d->move_queue, state,
-							   polarity)) {
-			if (d->move_queue->count >= 14) {
-				pr_info("[LYQ-damon-hall]:damon mechanism pushed by hand, abort\n");
-				hall_core_reset_queues();
-				cancel_vib_hrtimer(0);
-			} else {
-				cancel_vib_hrtimer(1);
-			}
+							   polarity) &&
+			   d->move_queue->count >= d->move_queue->size &&
+			   queue_data_is_move_press(d->move_queue)) {
+			/*
+			 * The divergence criterion on its own fires on a healthy
+			 * move: the up/down difference changes by far more than
+			 * 30 counts while the module travels, which aborted the
+			 * elevator after a few hundred milliseconds ("stopped
+			 * half way").  Only stop when the mechanism really has
+			 * stopped - a hand push or a blockage stalls it, while a
+			 * healthy move keeps both channels changing.
+			 */
+			pr_info("[LYQ-damon-hall]:damon mechanism blocked, abort\n");
+			hall_core_reset_queues();
+			cancel_vib_hrtimer(0);
 		}
 	}
 
diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/mxm1120.c b/drivers/input/misc/mxm1120.c
index db0ab5238..efb268724 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/mxm1120.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/mxm1120.c
@@ -233,19 +233,20 @@ static int m1120_set_operation_mode(struct m1120_data *d, bool measure)
 		return ret;
 
 	/*
-	 * [RE] Bit 0 is START and starting the conversion is what the factory
-	 * driver does, but on this ROM the hall samples then reach BBK's camera
-	 * service, which switches the elevator from its open loop timing to a
-	 * closed loop path that this kernel does not implement (the factory's
-	 * vib_pwm_state_move_sate / vib_pwm_state_init pair).  The elevator then
-	 * stops half way - "卡一半不升" - and the front camera is unusable.
+	 * [RE] The factory starts a conversion with bit 0 (START) set together
+	 * with bit 3, i.e. value 0x09, and clears bit 0 to stop.  Only the mode
+	 * bit 6 was written before, which leaves the part idle: the sensor
+	 * acknowledges (id 0x9c) and the register writes stick, but status bit 0
+	 * of the 0x10 block never becomes DRDY and every sample is refused.
 	 *
-	 * Until that path is ported, keep the sensors in standby as before: with
-	 * no valid samples (bbk_hall_data reports the -2000 failure value) the
-	 * service uses the time based move that works, and the camera raises
-	 * normally.  Set M1120_OP_START_SET below to restore the conversion.
+	 * The sensors used to be left idle on purpose, because once valid samples
+	 * reach BBK's camera service it switches the elevator to its own closed
+	 * loop path, which this reconstruction does not implement yet, and the
+	 * elevator then stops half way.  The samples are enabled again so that
+	 * path can be observed on the device; keep the working image at hand.
 	 */
-	v = measure ? (v | M1120_OP_MEASUREMENT) : (v & ~M1120_OP_MEASUREMENT);
+	v = measure ? (v | M1120_OP_MEASUREMENT | M1120_OP_START_SET)
+		    : (v & ~(M1120_OP_MEASUREMENT | M1120_OP_START));
 	ret = m1120_i2c_set_reg(d, M1120_REG_OPMODE, v);
 	dev_info(d->dev, "%s: %s, opmode 0x%02x\n", __func__,
 		 measure ? "start conversion" : "stop conversion", v);
